Phase 7 verification report. Scope git diff --name-only d61542e HEAD: 10 files - holdGate.ts (+12 tests), installHint.ts (+11), parentPanel.ts, parentPanelTypes.ts (DOM glue, exempt), main.ts wiring, index.html CSS, vitest.config.ts (hud coverage exemption recorded), plan.md. Gates: pnpm check biome 73 files clean, tsc --noEmit clean, CI=true pnpm test 366 tests across 29 files; coverage All files 82.58 stmts / 81.23 branch / 87.44 funcs / 82.44 lines.

Manual verification, driven through the real frame function because the tab's requestAnimationFrame is paused when the window is not visible: a two-second hold on the gear left the panel shut with the ring at 0.66 and back to 0 on release; three continuous seconds opened it (once per hold, not per frame); the sound toggle muted the engine and dimmed itself and restored both on a second press; the helper toggle switched the hand off; the cross closed the panel; console empty. The reviewer then played the same pass by hand on the build and confirmed all of it, plus the helper hand's mid-mission behaviour.

One fault found and fixed in this phase, again a wiring fault rather than a logic fault: the panel overlay was built and populated but never appended to the panel root, so querying it in the page returned null. That is the third phase running where driving the real frame/DOM caught something the unit tests could not see.

Caveat: the install hint's DOM layer was not verified in-page by the agent - this session's browser connection answered Vite module fetches with 502 Bad Gateway while the same URLs returned 200 over plain HTTP, so the app never booted there. Its decision, fade and platform sniff are covered by 11 tests, and the reviewer confirmed the element by eye in the manual pass. Deviations accepted by the reviewer: no music toggle (the game ships no music track, so the control would be dead) and no attribution in the UI (Kenney kits are CC0 and require none; product guidelines forbid written words anywhere in the interface, provenance stays in the kit and audio READMEs).
